<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="TexasHoldem.UI.Maui.MainPage"
             Shell.NavBarIsVisible="False"
             BackgroundColor="#2F151A">

    <!--
        Every AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds X and Y on the table surface below is
        copied verbatim from the Canvas.Left / Canvas.Top of the matching element in
        UI/TexasHoldem.UI.Wpf/MainWindow.xaml, except the sixteen deviations listed
        here, each with its reason. Do not adjust any of the others.

        PHASES 4 AND 5, approved 2026-09-10. The first two because the WPF sizes
        cannot hold the widest legal content, the third to centre the card text:

        - Hole card slots are 176 wide, not 150, and each X is shifted 13 to the left
          so the slot stays centred where it was tuned. At 150 a hand of two ten-rank
          cards clips to one card whenever either is a spade or a club, which covers
          five of the six pocket-tens combinations.
        - The centre panel sits at X 408, not 468, and its stack is 450 wide, not 360.
          At 360 a board holding three or more ten-rank cards drops the last card.
        - CardSlotLabelStyle carries TranslationY -5, because Android will not
          vertically centre text in a fixed-height box. See MauiProgram.cs too.

        The first two verified on device with the widest possible content:
        "10s 10h" in all eight seats and a board of "10s 10h 10d 10c Ks".

        PHASE 6, the touch pass, approved 2026-09-10. All chrome, none of it table:

        - The card-visibility and game-size pickers (WPF 20,66 and 21,93) are gone
          from the surface. Both are chosen from tiles in the settings sheet behind
          the gear at 1196,10, which is new.
        - The AI decision-log toggle (WPF canvas 20,-1) is removed on Android. So is
          the Show Raise check box from WPF's bottom-left overlay; Save on Exit,
          beside it there, was never ported.
        - The AI and Log toggles are 76 x 68 at 912,642 and 1188,642, up from 36 x 24
          and 48 x 24, to reach a 12 mm touch target. Both panels moved up with
          them and now end at Y 636, clear of the toggles.
        - StakesLabel at 21,63 is new. The stakes used to be readable from the
          game-size picker, which is no longer on the table.
        - The Raise button and its raise-amount box are removed from the action
          bar. Typing an amount pops a keyboard over the table; the pot-fraction
          buttons are the only raise path on Android. Windows keeps both.

        SESSION 8, the end-of-hand reveal, decided 2026-09-11. Neither is layout:

        - A masked seat is blank, and so is the board before the first round.
          WPF shows "?? ??" and "?? ?? ?? ?? ??"; eight of them on the felt read
          as clutter. Since session 9 MaskedCards in MauiTableView.cs is two card backs for a live seat and blank for a folded one.
        - Masked seats are revealed on the table when the hand ends, per the
          OTHER PLAYERS' CARDS tile in the settings sheet: SHOWDOWN reveals the
          seats that showed, ALL END reveals all eight. WPF never reveals on the
          table; its hand log is the only place the showdown cards appear.

        SESSION 9, decided 2026-09-11 from the user's play on the tablet:

        - The eight bet slots are 176 wide at the card slot's X, up from 110
          centred over it, so "RR   +16 (16)" no longer clips.
        - Seat 2's card slot and bet slot are at Y 298 and 263, 15 lower than
          WPF's 283 and 248, mirroring seat 7, because the widened seat 1 bet
          slot overlapped seat 2's.
        - The dealer button is 40 wide (WPF 26), sits on the card slot's outer
          end centred on its height (WPF: the slot's left edge in the bet row),
          and is hidden until the first deal and after a reset.
        - A folded seat's card slot is dimmed only while it shows cards; an
          empty slot is full strength. WPF dims from the fold on.
        - The bet label's hand total is always in parentheses: "X   (16)", not
          WPF's "X   16".

        SESSION 10, decided 2026-09-12 from the user's look at the tablet:

        - Every bet slot is 30 tall and touches its card slot: Y = card Y + 44
          for seats 1 and 8, card Y - 30 for the rest. The BetSlotBorderStyle
          3-unit top margin is gone. WPF keeps its 33-tall slots, its margin,
          and its uneven gaps.

        Where a WPF style carried Margin="0,3,0,0" on an absolutely positioned
        element, the Canvas value is kept as the X,Y here and the 3px is added to the
        bounds height instead, so the rendered box lands in the same place it does on
        Windows.
    -->

    <ContentPage.Resources>

        <Style x:Key="SeatBoxStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#B3121212" />
            <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="#664E4E4E" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeShape" Value="RoundRectangle 6" />
        </Style>

        <!-- WPF SeatTextBoxStyle, the shared chrome behind every seat text row. -->
        <Style x:Key="SlotBorderStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#22000000" />
            <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="#55282828" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="4,2" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,3,0,0" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeShape" Value="Rectangle" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="SeatStackLabelStyle" TargetType="Label">
            <Setter Property="LineBreakMode" Value="NoWrap" />
            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#FFF2F2F2" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="28" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalTextAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="SeatStatusLabelStyle" TargetType="Label">
            <Setter Property="LineBreakMode" Value="NoWrap" />
            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#FFDDDDDD" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="18" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalTextAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="CardSlotBorderStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#22000000" />
            <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="#55282828" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="6,0" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeShape" Value="RoundRectangle 3" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="CardSlotLabelStyle" TargetType="Label">
            <Setter Property="VerticalOptions" Value="Center" />
            <!-- Android draws this line box filling the whole slot with the glyphs at
                 its bottom and ~23 physical px of empty ascent space above. Gravity and
                 padding cannot reclaim that: padding clips the glyphs instead. A render
                 offset moves the text without touching layout. Measured, not guessed.

                 COUPLED TO MauiProgram.ConfigureLabelRendering. This -5 was calibrated
                 with Android's label font padding switched off. Remove that and this
                 value is wrong. Re-measure with Tools/measure_card_slot.py, which
                 should read 10px above and 9px below, before changing either one. -->
            <Setter Property="TranslationY" Value="-5" />
            <Setter Property="LineBreakMode" Value="NoWrap" />
            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#FFF2F2F2" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="36" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalTextAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalTextAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="BetSlotBorderStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#22000000" />
            <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="#55282828" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="4,2" />
            <!-- No margin. Until session 10 a 3-unit top margin here made every bet
                 slot draw 3 lower and 3 shorter than its LayoutBounds said, which is
                 why the gaps to the card slots were uneven and could not be read
                 from the coordinates. The bounds now say exactly where the box is.
                 SlotBorderStyle, for the seat info rows, keeps its margin. -->
            <Setter Property="StrokeShape" Value="Rectangle" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="BetSlotLabelStyle" TargetType="Label">
            <Setter Property="VerticalOptions" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="LineBreakMode" Value="NoWrap" />
            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#FFF2F2F2" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="18" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalTextAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalTextAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="CenterPanelStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#AA0E0E0E" />
            <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="#664E4E4E" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeShape" Value="RoundRectangle 8" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="CommunityCardBorderStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#77FFFFFF" />
            <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="#66FFFFFF" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="6,2" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,4,0,0" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeShape" Value="RoundRectangle 3" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="CommunityCardLabelStyle" TargetType="Label">
            <Setter Property="VerticalOptions" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="LineBreakMode" Value="NoWrap" />
            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#FFF2F2F2" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="40" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalTextAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <!--
            Phase 6, the settings sheet behind the gear. Every tile is 72 units
            tall: the surface scales by about 1.906 on the 2560 x 1600 emulator,
            so 72 units is 137 physical pixels, clear of the 130 px that is 12 mm
            on the tablet. The whole tile is the touch target, not the label in it.
        -->
        <Style x:Key="SettingsSectionStyle" TargetType="Label">
            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#B9A0A4" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="14" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="LineBreakMode" Value="NoWrap" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="ChoiceTileLabelStyle" TargetType="Label">
            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#8A7A7D" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="20" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="LineBreakMode" Value="NoWrap" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalOptions" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalOptions" Value="Center" />
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="ExtraButtonToggleStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="HeightRequest" Value="72" />
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#1C1416" />
            <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="#4D3A3E" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="2" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeShape">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <RoundRectangle CornerRadius="6" />
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <Style x:Key="LogPanelStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#141414" />
            <Setter Property="Stroke" Value="#333333" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="StrokeShape" Value="Rectangle" />
        </Style>

        <!-- PALETTE-BLOCK-START -->
        <!--
            Phase 6 action-bar palette.

            Seven roles, not five: the raise sizes split into the three groups
            the user asked for on 2026-09-10: below the pot, the pot itself,
            and above the pot, so the bar reads as a ramp rather than a row of
            identical amber buttons.

            No red anywhere. Red was tried on ALL IN and rejected: it reads as
            an error state, which is the wrong message at the moment the player
            is making the boldest move in the game.

            Colour carries two jobs at once: which action a button performs, and
            whether it is live right now. The Disabled visual state is what
            preserves the "it is your turn" signal that the stock template gave
            away for free by grey-ing everything out. Its grey is
            (200,200,200) on (20,20,20), sampled from the pre-palette build so
            the start screen looks exactly as it did.

            Next Hand is the one button whose colour means something other than
            which action it performs, because the action changes. During a hand
            it folds you and skips the showdown; once the hand is over it just
            deals the next one. SetNextHandHighlight already toggles at exactly
            those two moments, so gold is the safe state and the neutral grey is
            the "this does something you may not want" state. Pressing a big
            gold button should never muck a good hand.

            All four NextHand colours are read back by MainPage.xaml.cs in
            SetNextHandHighlight, and the four Fold and ButtonOff colours in
            PaintFoldButtons. If you rename them, fix those methods too. The
            settings sheet's Quit Game button references Fold* by StaticResource
            and follows a rename on its own. AllIn* is shared by ALL IN's Normal
            state and the sheet's Back to Game button, so the two greens cannot
            drift apart.
        -->
        <Color x:Key="FoldColor">#A34A55</Color>
        <Color x:Key="FoldTextColor">#FFF0F1</Color>
        <Color x:Key="ButtonOffColor">#C8C8C8</Color>
        <Color x:Key="ButtonOffTextColor">#141414</Color>
        <Color x:Key="NextHandColor">#5E5652</Color>
        <Color x:Key="NextHandTextColor">#EDE9E6</Color>
        <Color x:Key="NextHandGlowColor">#C8A34A</Color>
        <Color x:Key="NextHandGlowTextColor">#1A1A1A</Color>
        <Color x:Key="AllInColor">#2F7048</Color>
        <Color x:Key="AllInTextColor">#F0FCF4</Color>



        <Style x:Key="CallButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="HeightRequest" Value="66" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="ClassId" Value="BarButton" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="BorderWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups">
                <VisualStateGroupList>
                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#6E8AAE" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#F4F7FC" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#C8C8C8" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#141414" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                    </VisualStateGroup>
                </VisualStateGroupList>
            </Setter>
        </Style>


        <Style x:Key="RaiseLowButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="HeightRequest" Value="66" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="ClassId" Value="BarButton" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="BorderWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups">
                <VisualStateGroupList>
                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#2F7E92" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#F2FBFD" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#C8C8C8" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#141414" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                    </VisualStateGroup>
                </VisualStateGroupList>
            </Setter>
        </Style>


        <Style x:Key="PotButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="HeightRequest" Value="66" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="ClassId" Value="BarButton" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="BorderWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups">
                <VisualStateGroupList>
                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#3E8E5A" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#F2FFF6" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#C8C8C8" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#141414" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                    </VisualStateGroup>
                </VisualStateGroupList>
            </Setter>
        </Style>


        <Style x:Key="RaiseHighButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="HeightRequest" Value="66" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="ClassId" Value="BarButton" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="BorderWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups">
                <VisualStateGroupList>
                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#2C4C70" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#EDF2F9" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#C8C8C8" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#141414" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                    </VisualStateGroup>
                </VisualStateGroupList>
            </Setter>
        </Style>


        <Style x:Key="AllInButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="HeightRequest" Value="66" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="ClassId" Value="BarButton" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="BorderWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups">
                <VisualStateGroupList>
                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource AllInColor}" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="{StaticResource AllInTextColor}" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled">
                            <VisualState.Setters>
                                <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="#C8C8C8" />
                                <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#141414" />
                            </VisualState.Setters>
                        </VisualState>
                    </VisualStateGroup>
                </VisualStateGroupList>
            </Setter>
        </Style>


        <Style x:Key="NextHandButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="HeightRequest" Value="66" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="ClassId" Value="BarButton" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="BorderWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="BackgroundColor" Value="{StaticResource NextHandColor}" />
            <Setter Property="TextColor" Value="#EDE9E6" />
        </Style>

        <!--
            Both Fold buttons use this style, and it carries no colours of its
            own. Between hands they are a special case: still tappable, so Fold
            keeps advancing the hand, but painted as inactive so they do not
            compete with Next Hand. A visual state with colours would fight
            that, because MAUI applies the Normal state after IsEnabled is set
            and would repaint the button red. PaintFoldButtons in
            MainPage.xaml.cs owns the colours in every state.

            The empty CommonStates group is deliberate and load-bearing. Without
            it the implicit Button style in Styles.xaml supplies its own group,
            whose Disabled state is theme-bound: light grey in light mode, near
            black (#404040) in dark mode. That state outranks the colours set
            from code, so on a tablet in dark mode the disabled Fold went almost
            black while the enabled one between hands stayed light grey. The
            emulator runs in light mode, where the two happen to coincide.
            Found by the 2026-09-11 review.
        -->
        <Style x:Key="FoldTappableButtonStyle" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="HeightRequest" Value="66" />
            <Setter Property="FontAttributes" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="ClassId" Value="BarButton" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="6" />
            <Setter Property="BorderWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="VisualStateManager.VisualStateGroups">
                <VisualStateGroupList>
                    <VisualStateGroup x:Name="CommonStates">
                        <VisualState x:Name="Normal" />
                        <VisualState x:Name="Disabled" />
                    </VisualStateGroup>
                </VisualStateGroupList>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <!-- PALETTE-BLOCK-END -->

    </ContentPage.Resources>

    <Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto">

        <Grid x:Name="TableHost" Grid.Row="0" SizeChanged="TableHost_SizeChanged">
            <Grid.Background>
                <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
                    <GradientStop Color="#2F151A" Offset="0" />
                    <GradientStop Color="#31161B" Offset="0.5" />
                    <GradientStop Color="#2F151A" Offset="1" />
                </LinearGradientBrush>
            </Grid.Background>

            <!-- The 1280x720 design surface. Scaled uniformly in TableHost_SizeChanged
                 and centred, which is what the WPF Viewbox with Stretch="Uniform" does.
                 The letterbox bands show the gradient above. -->
            <Grid x:Name="DesignSurface"
                  WidthRequest="1280"
                  HeightRequest="720"
                  HorizontalOptions="Center"
                  VerticalOptions="Center">

                <Image Source="cardtable.png" Aspect="Fill" />

                <AbsoluteLayout x:Name="TableLayout">

                    <!--
                        Top-left chrome. On Windows the card-visibility and
                        game-size pickers and the AI decision-log toggle also sit
                        here. Phase 6 took all three off the table: the pickers
                        became tiles in the settings sheet behind the gear at top
                        right, and the decision-log toggle was removed. Neither
                        picker could reach 12 mm here: only 174 units of column
                        are clear above the seat 7 box, and two 12 mm pickers plus
                        captions need about 180.
                    -->
                    <Label x:Name="HandCounterLabel"
                           AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="20,14,AutoSize,AutoSize"
                           Text="Hands: 0" TextColor="#E6E6E6" FontSize="18" FontAttributes="Bold" />

                    <Label x:Name="BuyInCounterLabel"
                           AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="21,40,AutoSize,AutoSize"
                           Text="Buy-Ins: 1" TextColor="#E6E6E6" FontSize="16" />

                    <!--
                        Phase 6. The stakes used to be readable from the game-size
                        picker sitting here on the table. That picker became tiles in
                        the settings sheet, which left no way to see what game you are
                        playing, so the value is echoed here as plain text.
                    -->
                    <Label x:Name="StakesLabel"
                           AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="21,63,AutoSize,AutoSize"
                           Text="Stakes: 1/2" TextColor="#E6E6E6" FontSize="16"
                           LineBreakMode="NoWrap" />

                    <!-- Seat info boxes -->
                    <Border x:Name="Seat1InfoBorder" Style="{StaticResource SeatBoxStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="756,4,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="150">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat1NameLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Player 1" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat1StackLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="0" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat1StatusLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Waiting" /></Border>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <Border x:Name="Seat2InfoBorder" Style="{StaticResource SeatBoxStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="1106,184,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="150">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat2NameLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Player 2" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat2StackLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="0" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat2StatusLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Waiting" /></Border>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <Border x:Name="Seat3InfoBorder" Style="{StaticResource SeatBoxStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="1106,396,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="150">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat3NameLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Player 3" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat3StackLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="0" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat3StatusLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Waiting" /></Border>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <Border x:Name="Seat4InfoBorder" Style="{StaticResource SeatBoxStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="744,587,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="150">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat4NameLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Player 4" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat4StackLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="0" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat4StatusLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Waiting" /></Border>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <Border x:Name="Seat5InfoBorder" Style="{StaticResource SeatBoxStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="409,587,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="150">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat5NameLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Player 5" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat5StackLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="0" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat5StatusLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Waiting" /></Border>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <Border x:Name="Seat6InfoBorder" Style="{StaticResource SeatBoxStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="10,440,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="150">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat6NameLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Player 6" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat6StackLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="0" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat6StatusLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Waiting" /></Border>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <Border x:Name="Seat7InfoBorder" Style="{StaticResource SeatBoxStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="10,174,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="150">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat7NameLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Player 7" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat7StackLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="0" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat7StatusLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Waiting" /></Border>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <Border x:Name="Seat8InfoBorder" Style="{StaticResource SeatBoxStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="362,4,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="150">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat8NameLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Player 8" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat8StackLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="0" /></Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}"><Label x:Name="Seat8StatusLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStatusLabelStyle}" Text="Waiting" /></Border>
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <!-- Centre panel: board, pot, turn info -->
                    <Border Style="{StaticResource CenterPanelStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="408,280,AutoSize,AutoSize">
                        <VerticalStackLayout WidthRequest="450">
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource CommunityCardBorderStyle}">
                                <Label x:Name="CommunityCardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CommunityCardLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                            </Border>
                            <Border Style="{StaticResource SlotBorderStyle}">
                                <Label x:Name="PotLabel" Style="{StaticResource SeatStackLabelStyle}" Text="Pot: 0" />
                            </Border>
                            <Label x:Name="TurnInfoLabel" Margin="2,6,2,0" TextColor="#E6E6E6" FontSize="20"
                                   HorizontalTextAlignment="Center" LineBreakMode="NoWrap" Text="Waiting for game start..." />
                        </VerticalStackLayout>
                    </Border>

                    <!-- Hole card slots, 176 x 44. Windows uses 150; see the header. -->
                    <Border x:Name="Seat1CardsBorder" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="743,185,176,44">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat1CardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat2CardsBorder" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="884,298,176,44">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat2CardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat3CardsBorder" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="884,399,176,44">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat3CardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat4CardsBorder" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="731,490,176,44">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat4CardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat5CardsBorder" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="410,490,176,44">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat5CardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat6CardsBorder" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="229,421,176,44">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat6CardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat7CardsBorder" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="229,298,176,44">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat7CardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat8CardsBorder" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="364,185,176,44">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat8CardsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>

                    <!--
                        Bet labels. Were 110 wide, centred over the 176 card slots; widened to the
                        slot width in session 9 so "RR   +16 (16)" no longer clips. That made seat 1's
                        slot overlap seat 2's, so seat 2's card slot and bet slot moved down 15 to
                        mirror seat 7's.

                        Session 10, 2026-09-12: every bet slot is 30 tall and touches its card slot,
                        so the pair reads as one box with a line across it. Seats 1 and 8 have the
                        bet slot under the cards (Y = card Y + 44); the other six have it above
                        (Y = card Y - 30). Before this the gaps were 0, 6 and 4 physical pixels on
                        the tablet for seats 1, 8 and the rest, because the style's 3-unit top
                        margin (now removed) shifted the drawn box. Seat 1's slot ends at 259 and
                        seat 2's starts at 268, seat 8's ends at 259 and seat 7's starts at 268:
                        9 clear in both overlapping columns.
                    -->
                    <Border x:Name="Seat1BetBorder" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="743,229,176,30">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat1BetLabel" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat2BetBorder" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="884,268,176,30">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat2BetLabel" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat3BetBorder" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="884,369,176,30">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat3BetLabel" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat4BetBorder" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="731,460,176,30">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat4BetLabel" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat5BetBorder" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="410,460,176,30">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat5BetLabel" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat6BetBorder" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="229,391,176,30">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat6BetLabel" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat7BetBorder" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="229,268,176,30">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat7BetLabel" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>
                    <Border x:Name="Seat8BetBorder" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotBorderStyle}" AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="364,229,176,30">
                        <Label x:Name="Seat8BetLabel" Style="{StaticResource BetSlotLabelStyle}" Text="" />
                    </Border>

                    <!--
                        Dealer button. Placed and shown by MauiTableView.SetDealerSeat at the
                        first deal; hidden until then, because at 40 wide (session 9) its
                        placeholder position was a visible blob on the rail before the game.
                    -->
                    <Ellipse x:Name="DealerButton" IsVisible="False"
                             AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="835,125,40,40"
                             Fill="#E6E0AA" Stroke="#1A1A1A" StrokeThickness="2" />

                    <!--
                        The two overlay panels and their toggles. WPF positions these in
                        code from the toggles' measured bounds; the Phase 4 port resolved
                        that arithmetic once against the fixed 1280x720 surface.

                        Phase 6 enlarged both toggles to 76 x 68 at Y 642 for a 12 mm
                        target, so both panels now end at Y 636, 6 above the toggles.
                        Left where the old small toggles put them, an open panel covered
                        its own toggle. Found by the cold-read doc review, 2026-09-10.

                        2026-09-11, the user's decision: the Log toggle is hidden on
                        Android, not removed. The panel, the log writes and the
                        Windows code are untouched, so it can come back by deleting
                        one IsVisible. The AI panel moved into the corner the Log
                        toggle vacated: right of the AI toggle (which ends at X 988),
                        below the seat 3 box (which ends at Y 526), out to the right
                        margin and down to the toggles' bottom edge, 6 units clear
                        on each side. It used to cover seat 3's last-action line;
                        now it covers nothing.
                    -->
                    <Button x:Name="AiRecommendationToggle"
                            AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="912,642,76,68"
                            Text="AI" FontSize="17" FontAttributes="Bold" Padding="0"
                            BackgroundColor="#141414" BorderColor="#333333" BorderWidth="1" TextColor="#E6E6E6"
                            Clicked="AiRecommendationToggle_Clicked" />

                    <Border x:Name="AiRecommendationPanel"
                            Style="{StaticResource LogPanelStyle}"
                            AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="994,532,270,178"
                            IsVisible="False">
                        <Label x:Name="AiRecommendationLabel" Padding="10,6,6,4" FontSize="16" BackgroundColor="#101010"
                               TextColor="#E6E6E6" Text="AI recommendations will appear here." />
                    </Border>

                    <Button x:Name="ActionLogToggle"
                            AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="1188,642,76,68"
                            IsVisible="False"
                            Text="Log" FontSize="17" FontAttributes="Bold" Padding="0"
                            BackgroundColor="#141414" BorderColor="#333333" BorderWidth="1" TextColor="#E6E6E6"
                            Clicked="ActionLogToggle_Clicked" />

                    <Border x:Name="ActionLogPanel"
                            Style="{StaticResource LogPanelStyle}"
                            AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="934,0,330,636"
                            IsVisible="False">
                        <ScrollView x:Name="ActionLogScroll" Padding="6,4" BackgroundColor="#101010">
                            <Label x:Name="ActionLogLabel" FontSize="12" TextColor="#E6E6E6" Text="" />
                        </ScrollView>
                    </Border>

                    <!--
                        The gear and its sheet are declared last so they paint
                        over the action log panel, which occupies the same
                        top-right corner when it is open.
                    -->
                    <Button x:Name="SettingsButton"
                            AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="1196,10,68,68"
                            Text="&#x2699;&#xFE0E;"
                            FontSize="32"
                            Padding="0"
                            BackgroundColor="#141414" BorderColor="#4D3A3E" BorderWidth="2"
                            TextColor="#E6E6E6" CornerRadius="8"
                            Clicked="SettingsButton_Clicked" />

                    <Grid x:Name="SettingsOverlay"
                          AbsoluteLayout.LayoutBounds="0,0,1280,720"
                          BackgroundColor="#D9000000"
                          IsVisible="False">

                        <Grid.GestureRecognizers>
                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="SettingsOverlay_Tapped" />
                        </Grid.GestureRecognizers>

                        <Border WidthRequest="640" HeightRequest="660"
                                HorizontalOptions="Center" VerticalOptions="Center"
                                BackgroundColor="#150C0E" Stroke="#664E4E4E" StrokeThickness="2"
                                Padding="20">
                            <Border.StrokeShape>
                                <RoundRectangle CornerRadius="10" />
                            </Border.StrokeShape>

                            <!-- Swallow taps so they do not reach the scrim and close the sheet. -->
                            <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                <TapGestureRecognizer />
                            </Border.GestureRecognizers>

                            <VerticalStackLayout Spacing="0">

                                <!--
                                    The title row. Quit Game sits at the right of the title,
                                    away from Back to Game, so a tap meant for one cannot land
                                    on the other. It closes the app outright: the activity
                                    finishes and MainActivity.OnDestroy ends the process, so
                                    the player never has to learn Android's Back, Home or
                                    recents gestures to put the game away. 220 x 72 keeps the
                                    12 mm tap size with room for the two words. Moved here
                                    2026-09-11; it read "Quit" until session 9, which the user
                                    found could be taken as "quit settings".
                                -->
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" HeightRequest="72">
                                    <Label Grid.Column="0" Text="Settings" TextColor="#F2F2F2" FontSize="27"
                                           FontAttributes="Bold" LineBreakMode="NoWrap" VerticalOptions="Center" />
                                    <Button x:Name="QuitButton" Grid.Column="1" Text="Quit Game" Margin="0"
                                            WidthRequest="220" HeightRequest="72" VerticalOptions="Center"
                                            FontSize="19" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                            BackgroundColor="{StaticResource FoldColor}"
                                            TextColor="{StaticResource FoldTextColor}" CornerRadius="8"
                                            Clicked="QuitButton_Clicked" />
                                </Grid>

                                <!--
                                    One three-way choice. ALWAYS shows every seat all hand;
                                    SHOWDOWN and ALL END mask the other seats during the hand
                                    and reveal them when it ends, the showdown seats or all
                                    eight. The caption carries the meaning so the tiles stay
                                    short. Decided 2026-09-11.
                                -->
                                <Label Text="OTHER PLAYERS' CARDS" Style="{StaticResource SettingsSectionStyle}" Margin="0,28,0,4" />
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                    <Border x:Name="CardAlwaysTile" Grid.Column="0" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="CardAlwaysTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="CardAlwaysTileLabel" Text="ALWAYS" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="CardShowdownTile" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="CardShowdownTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="CardShowdownTileLabel" Text="SHOWDOWN" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="CardAllEndTile" Grid.Column="2" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="CardAllEndTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="CardAllEndTileLabel" Text="ALL END" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                </Grid>

                                <Label x:Name="StakesSectionLabel" Text="STAKES" Style="{StaticResource SettingsSectionStyle}" Margin="0,10,0,4" />
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*,*" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8" RowSpacing="8">
                                    <Border x:Name="StakeOneTile" Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="StakeOneTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="StakeOneTileLabel" Text="1/2" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="StakeTwoTile" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="StakeTwoTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="StakeTwoTileLabel" Text="2/4" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="StakeFiveTile" Grid.Column="2" Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="StakeFiveTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="StakeFiveTileLabel" Text="5/10" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="StakeTenTile" Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="1" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="StakeTenTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="StakeTenTileLabel" Text="10/20" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="StakeFiftyTile" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="StakeFiftyTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="StakeFiftyTileLabel" Text="50/100" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="StakeHundredTile" Grid.Column="2" Grid.Row="1" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="StakeHundredTile_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="StakeHundredTileLabel" Text="100/200" Style="{StaticResource ChoiceTileLabelStyle}" />
                                    </Border>
                                </Grid>

                                <Label Text="EXTRA RAISE BUTTONS" Style="{StaticResource SettingsSectionStyle}" Margin="0,12,0,4" />
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*,*,*" ColumnSpacing="8">
                                    <Border x:Name="OneThirdToggle" Grid.Column="0" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="OneThirdToggle_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="OneThirdToggleLabel" Text="1/3" TextColor="#8A7A7D" FontSize="21" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                               HorizontalOptions="Center" VerticalOptions="Center" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="TwoThirdsToggle" Grid.Column="1" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="TwoThirdsToggle_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="TwoThirdsToggleLabel" Text="2/3" TextColor="#8A7A7D" FontSize="21" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                               HorizontalOptions="Center" VerticalOptions="Center" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="OnePointFiveToggle" Grid.Column="2" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="OnePointFiveToggle_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="OnePointFiveToggleLabel" Text="1.5X" TextColor="#8A7A7D" FontSize="21" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                               HorizontalOptions="Center" VerticalOptions="Center" />
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border x:Name="ThreeXToggle" Grid.Column="3" Style="{StaticResource ExtraButtonToggleStyle}">
                                        <Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                            <TapGestureRecognizer Tapped="ThreeXToggle_Tapped" />
                                        </Border.GestureRecognizers>
                                        <Label x:Name="ThreeXToggleLabel" Text="3X" TextColor="#8A7A7D" FontSize="21" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                               HorizontalOptions="Center" VerticalOptions="Center" />
                                    </Border>
                                </Grid>

                                <!--
                                    Back to Game and Quit Game are painted in the action bar's
                                    own colours, ALL IN green and Fold red, so they read as
                                    buttons and not as two more setting tiles, and green
                                    against red says which one is safe. Quit Game is in the
                                    title row at the top of the sheet; it used to sit right
                                    under this button, where a tap meant for it could close the
                                    app. The gap above separates the last row of tiles from the
                                    button. Asked for by the user 2026-09-11. This button was
                                    gold and read "Done" until session 9.
                                -->
                                <Button x:Name="SettingsDoneButton" Text="Back to Game" Margin="0,48,0,0"
                                        HeightRequest="76" FontSize="21" FontAttributes="Bold"
                                        BackgroundColor="{StaticResource AllInColor}"
                                        TextColor="{StaticResource AllInTextColor}" CornerRadius="8"
                                        Clicked="SettingsDoneButton_Clicked" />

                            </VerticalStackLayout>
                        </Border>
                    </Grid>

                </AbsoluteLayout>
            </Grid>
        </Grid>

        <!-- The action bar, below the scaled surface as on Windows. LayoutActionBar
             in MainPage.xaml.cs sizes every button at runtime; read it before
             changing anything here. -->
        <Border x:Name="ActionBarHost" Grid.Row="1" BackgroundColor="#141414" Stroke="#333333"
                StrokeThickness="0" Padding="6" SizeChanged="ActionBarHost_SizeChanged">
            <HorizontalStackLayout x:Name="ActionBar" HorizontalOptions="Center" VerticalOptions="Center">
                <Button x:Name="FoldLeftButton" Text="Fold" Style="{StaticResource FoldTappableButtonStyle}" Clicked="FoldButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="CheckCallButton" Text="Check/Call" Style="{StaticResource CallButtonStyle}" Clicked="CheckCallButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="OneThirdPotButton" Text="1/3" Style="{StaticResource RaiseLowButtonStyle}" IsVisible="False" Clicked="OneThirdPotButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="HalfPotButton" Text="1/2" Style="{StaticResource RaiseLowButtonStyle}" Clicked="HalfPotButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="TwoThirdsPotButton" Text="2/3" Style="{StaticResource RaiseLowButtonStyle}" IsVisible="False" Clicked="TwoThirdsPotButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="PotButton" Text="POT" Style="{StaticResource PotButtonStyle}" Clicked="PotButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="OnePointFivePotButton" Text="1.5X" Style="{StaticResource RaiseHighButtonStyle}" IsVisible="False" Clicked="OnePointFivePotButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="TwoXPotButton" Text="2X" Style="{StaticResource RaiseHighButtonStyle}" Clicked="TwoXPotButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="ThreeXPotButton" Text="3X" Style="{StaticResource RaiseHighButtonStyle}" IsVisible="False" Clicked="ThreeXPotButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="AllInButton" Text="ALL IN" Style="{StaticResource AllInButtonStyle}" Clicked="AllInButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="CheckCallRightButton" Text="Check/Call" Style="{StaticResource CallButtonStyle}" Clicked="CheckCallButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="FoldButton" Text="Fold" Style="{StaticResource FoldTappableButtonStyle}" Clicked="FoldButton_Clicked" />
                <Button x:Name="NextHandButton" Text="Start Game" Style="{StaticResource NextHandButtonStyle}"
                        Clicked="NextHandButton_Clicked" />
            </HorizontalStackLayout>
        </Border>

    </Grid>

</ContentPage>
